Project: Nemesis, a keyboard-driven cockpit for Claude Code on Electron and TypeScript that grows into a Nyxt-style browser. Read CLAUDE.md first, then README.org. Read SECURITY.org before any change under src/main/security/, src/preload/ or src/main/agent/.

Issue #43 is the plan. Work only issues that carry a milestone, the `queue-ready` label, and no `needs-pedro` label.

## Conventions for every issue

- One branch per issue (`claude-queue/<number>`), or one stack branch for a `--stack` run, and one draft pull request (the queue is unattended, so the pull request is its review surface; interactive sessions commit to main directly). Small commits with a Conventional Commits prefix. Explain why, not what.
- Run `npm run gate` before every commit once package.json exists. Do not open the pull request for review with a red gate.
- When the work is done: tick the issue checklist, strike abandoned items with a reason, bold anything that remains, post a one-line "verified with ..." comment naming the commands and specs, and label `claude-queue:solved`. If blocked, label `needs-pedro` with the exact question and stop.
- Never add a dependency without a one-line justification in the pull request. Never add a dependency that needs a lifecycle script.

## Security

- Security-labeled issues and anything touching src/main/security/, src/preload/, the permission bridge or tests/e2e/security/ may be implemented by the queue but are merged only after interactive review by Pedro. Say so in the pull request description.
- Controls are test-first. The failing spec lands in the same pull request.
- Never log tokens, cookies, page content or prompts outside the session folder.

## Do not

- Do not run installers that prompt. `npm ci --ignore-scripts` then `node node_modules/electron/install.js` is the only install path.
- Do not change keymaps, on-disk formats or the security policy to make a test pass. Ask instead.
- Do not port code from ~/projects/nyxt. Read it for ideas, cite the file in the ADR, write TypeScript.
